Mālyavān turns and rebukes slaughter of fleeing --- Viṣṇu vows gods safety and Rākṣasa death --- Mālyavān spears lotus-eyed chest --- Viṣṇu hurls back spear into broad chest --- Mālyavān lances chest and punches god --- Sky cheers his strikes on Viṣṇu and Garuḍa --- Garuḍa wing wind sweeps Mālyavān away --- Shamed brothers flee to Laṅkā then Pātāla --- Agastya names Rāma eternal four-armed Nārāyaṇa